I wait at the counter.
He makes my coffee.
He puts a hot cup of coffee on a wooden tray.
He also puts a small plate on the tray.
My cinnamon roll is on the plate.
It smells lovely.
"Here you go, your order," he says.
"Thank you very much," I reply.
"Thank you for the good service."
"You are welcome," he says kindly.
I take the tray with both hands.
I walk very carefully across the floor.
I walk back to my table by the window.
I put the tray down on the table.
Now I would like to sit down.
I am ready for a good break.
